<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Afzal Khan (general)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1659">1659</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Afzal Khan was a leading general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shahi-dynasty">Bijapur Sultanate</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-adil-shah-ii">Ali Adil Shah II</a>. In 1659 he was sent with a large army to destroy the rising power of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a>, and at a meeting arranged below the fort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pratapgad">Pratapgad</a> he was killed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> leader, whose troops then routed the Bijapuri army. The encounter became one of the best-known episodes of Maratha history and tradition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/afzal-khan-general.jpg" alt="Afzal Khan (general)" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Afzul_Khan_-_Early_20th_Century.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
